{"outcome":"compromise","summary":"I built a small shelf unit with two drawers. It can't be rated for 50 kg: the configurator only checks that parts fit and don't collide, and knows nothing about strength or loads.

The unit is two storeys high. Each storey has a full hex base in the middle with a south-half base on each side. The two lower half bases each hold a drawer. The open faces are capped with solid end caps and the joints are bolted. Three covers make a flat top shelf 160 mm off the bench, and I put a row of books on it to show it in use. A stack of books and a single book didn't fit beside the row on the narrow top, so I left them off.

The build check passed with no issues and the mesh-collision check reads clear. It comes to 53 parts, about 2,527 g of filament and roughly 3,761 minutes (about 63 hours) of printing. Before trusting it with a heavy load of books, you'd need to load-test the printed parts in your chosen material.","requirements":[{"requirement":"Shelf unit for books","status":"met","evidence":"Two storeys of hex bases with top covers that make a 160 mm high shelf top; a row of books stands on it (prop:1). The build check passed and the mesh-collision check reads clear."},{"requirement":"Two drawers","status":"met","evidence":"drawer:0#-1,0#cut and drawer:0#1,0#cut sit on the cut faces of the two lower half bases."},{"requirement":"Rated to hold 50 kg of books","status":"unmet","evidence":"The configurator checks fit and collisions only. It has no load or strength rating, so the 50 kg capacity can't be verified or claimed. That depends on the print material and settings, and on load testing."}]}
